        "# 1. Introduction to Hugging Face Hub\n",
        "\n",
        "## What is Hugging Face Hub?\n",
        "\n",
        "Hugging Face Hub is a centralized platform for hosting, discovering, sharing and managing machine learning resources.\n",
        "\n",
        "It provides repositories containing:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Pretrained models\n",
        "- Tokenizers\n",
        "- Datasets\n",
        "- Model configurations\n",
        "- Fine-tuned models\n",
        "- Model documentation and metadata\n",
        "\n",
        "It provides a standardized ecosystem for working with different machine learning architectures.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why do we use Hugging Face Hub?\n",
        "\n",
        "Instead of manually downloading model weights, writing architecture-specific loading code and configuring tokenizers, we can use the Hugging Face ecosystem to access these resources through standardized APIs.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, we can load different compatible language models using:\n",
        "\n",
        "- AutoTokenizer\n",
        "- AutoConfig\n",
        "- AutoModel\n",
        "- AutoModelForCausalLM\n",
        "\n",
        "## Important components\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Hugging Face Hub:** Hosts model and dataset repositories.\n",
        "2. **Hugging Face Hub Python library:** Provides APIs to search, inspect and download repository contents.\n",
        "3. **Transformers:** Provides model architectures, tokenizers and training/inference utilities.\n",
        "4. **Datasets:** Provides tools to load and process datasets.\n",
        "5. **PEFT:** Provides parameter-efficient fine-tuning techniques such as LoRA.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Important distinction\n",
        "\n",
        "Hugging Face Hub and Transformers are not the same thing.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Hub is the platform and repository infrastructure.\n",
        "- Transformers is the Python library used to work with models and tokenizers.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Hub can host models that do not use Transformers, and Transformers can also load models from local directories.\n",
        ":::"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Gw53cLl0diFs"
      }
