        "# 5. Inspecting Model Information\n",
        "\n",
        "The `HfApi.model_info()` method retrieves metadata about a specific model repository.\n",
        "\n",
        "It returns a `ModelInfo` object.\n",
        "\n",
        "Important information available includes:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `modelId`: Full repository identifier.\n",
        "- `pipeline_tag`: Associated task or pipeline.\n",
        "- `downloads`: Download count.\n",
        "- `likes`: Number of likes.\n",
        "- `library_name`: Associated library, when available.\n",
        "- `tags`: Repository tags.\n",
        "- `gated`: Whether access is restricted.\n",
        "- `private`: Whether the repository is private.\n",
        "- `sha`: Commit revision identifier.\n",
        "- `lastModified`: Last modification timestamp.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why inspect a model first?\n",
        "\n",
        "Different models have different architectures, licenses, hardware requirements and supported tasks.\n",
        "\n",
        "Inspecting repository metadata helps us decide whether a model is suitable before downloading its weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Best practice:** Record the model's repository ID and commit SHA when building reproducible ML workflows."
