        "# 7. Downloading Individual Repository Files\n",
        "\n",
        "The Hugging Face Hub library provides `hf_hub_download()` to download an individual file from a repository.\n",
        "\n",
        "Important parameters:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `repo_id`: Repository identifier.\n",
        "- `filename`: File to download.\n",
        "- `revision`: Branch, tag or commit SHA.\n",
        "- `local_dir`: Optional destination directory.\n",
        "\n",
        "The function returns the local filesystem path of the downloaded file.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why use individual downloads?\n",
        "\n",
        "Sometimes we only need a model's configuration, tokenizer files or documentation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Downloading individual files avoids downloading unnecessary model weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Hub library also maintains a local cache, which helps avoid repeated downloads of unchanged files.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Important distinction:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- `hf_hub_download()` downloads an individual file.\n",
        "- `snapshot_download()` downloads a repository snapshot, potentially including model weights.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IKdFazq4pf-8"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
