      "source": [
        "# 8. Understanding Model Architecture Using AutoConfig\n",
        "\n",
        "`AutoConfig` is a Hugging Face Transformers class that automatically identifies the appropriate model configuration class based on the repository's configuration.\n",
        "\n",
        "It allows us to inspect different model architectures using a common interface.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Main method\n",
        "\n",
        "`AutoConfig.from_pretrained()`\n",
        "\n",
        "Important parameters:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `pretrained_model_name_or_path`: Model repository ID or local directory.\n",
        "- `revision`: Specific repository version.\n",
        "- `trust_remote_code`: Whether to allow custom repository code.\n",
        "- `cache_dir`: Optional custom cache location.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Important configuration attributes\n",
        "\n",
        "Depending on the architecture, configuration objects may contain:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `model_type`: Model architecture family.\n",
        "- `architectures`: Associated model architecture class names.\n",
        "- `hidden_size`: Hidden representation dimension.\n",
        "- `num_hidden_layers`: Number of transformer layers.\n",
        "- `num_attention_heads`: Number of attention heads.\n",
        "- `num_key_value_heads`: Number of key-value heads, when applicable.\n",
        "- `vocab_size`: Vocabulary size.\n",
        "- `max_position_embeddings`: Maximum position embedding capacity, when applicable.\n",
        "- `is_encoder_decoder`: Whether the architecture uses an encoder-decoder structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why AutoConfig is important\n",
        "\n",
        "It allows us to discover model architecture information before loading the actual weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is useful for:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Model selection.\n",
        "2. Hardware planning.\n",
        "3. Architecture discovery.\n",
        "4. Model compatibility checks.\n",
        "5. Building reusable model-loading pipelines.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Important:** Not every architecture uses the same configuration attributes. Always check whether an attribute exists before accessing it."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1-s54w-ur64N"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(\n",
        "    model_id,\n",
        "    revision=info.sha,\n",
