        "# 9. Model Cards and Model Metadata\n",
        "\n",
        "A model card is documentation associated with a Hugging Face model repository.\n",
        "\n",
        "It provides information about the model's intended purpose, training methodology, limitations and usage.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Important information to inspect\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Model architecture.\n",
        "2. Model size and parameter count.\n",
        "3. Supported tasks.\n",
        "4. Training data and methodology.\n",
        "5. License and usage restrictions.\n",
        "6. Intended applications.\n",
        "7. Known limitations.\n",
        "8. Recommended inference settings.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why model cards matter\n",
        "\n",
        "A model's technical compatibility does not automatically mean it is legally or practically suitable for a project.\n",
        "\n",
        "Before using a model, verify:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Whether its license permits your intended usage.\n",
        "- Whether commercial usage is allowed, if relevant.\n",
        "- Whether the model is gated.\n",
        "- Whether the model is suitable for your target task.\n",
        "- Whether its limitations create risks for your application.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Best practice:** Treat the model card as part of the model-selection process, not optional reading.\n",
        ":::For our selected model:\n",
        "\n",
        "Open Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct model repository\n",
        "\n",
        "Read its README and inspect its configuration."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ns0poa0wvovT"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from huggingface_hub import HfApi\n",
        "from transformers import AutoConfig\n",
        "\n",
        "api = HfApi()\n",
        "\n",
        "def inspect_model(repo_id):\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "    print(\"MODEL INSPECTION\")\n",
        "    print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 1. Fetch repository information\n",
        "\n",
        "    info = api.model_info(repo_id)\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nMODEL INFORMATION\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"Repository:\", info.modelId)\n",
        "    print(\"Task:\", info.pipeline_tag)\n",
        "    print(\"Downloads:\", info.downloads)\n",
        "    print(\"Likes:\", info.likes)\n",
        "    print(\"Library:\", info.library_name)\n",
        "    print(\"Gated:\", info.gated)\n",
        "    print(\"Revision:\", info.sha)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 2. List repository files\n",
        "\n",
        "    files = api.list_repo_files(\n",
        "        repo_id=repo_id,\n",
        "        repo_type=\"model\",\n",
        "        revision=info.sha\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nREPOSITORY FILES\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    for file in files:\n",
        "        print(file)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # 3. Load architecture configuration\n",
        "\n",
        "    config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(\n",
        "        repo_id,\n",
        "        revision=info.sha,\n",
        "        trust_remote_code=False\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nARCHITECTURE INFORMATION\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"Model Type:\", config.model_type)\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"Architecture:\",\n",
        "        getattr(config, \"architectures\", None)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"Hidden Size:\",\n",
        "        get_config_value(\n",
        "            config,\n",
        "            \"hidden_size\",\n",
        "            \"n_embd\",\n",
        "            \"d_model\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"Layers:\",\n",
        "        get_config_value(\n",
        "            config,\n",
        "            \"num_hidden_layers\",\n",
        "            \"n_layer\",\n",
        "            \"num_layers\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"Attention Heads:\",\n",
        "        get_config_value(\n",
        "            config,\n",
        "            \"num_attention_heads\",\n",
        "            \"n_head\",\n",
        "            \"num_heads\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"Vocabulary:\",\n",
        "        getattr(config, \"vocab_size\", None)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"Encoder Decoder:\",\n",
        "        getattr(config, \"is_encoder_decoder\", None)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nINSPECTION COMPLETED\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"info\": info,\n",
        "        \"files\": files,\n",
        "        \"config\": config,\n",
        "        \"revision\": info.sha\n",
        "    }"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "R9M9h2vQvzIb"
      },
      "execution_count": 21,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def get_config_value(config, *keys):\n",
        "    for key in keys:\n",
        "        if hasattr(config, key):\n",
        "            return getattr(config, key)\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "model_data = inspect_model(\n",
